  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Traeger entered its peak selling season with encouraging underlying demand, as year-to-date consumer sell-through trends were tracking slightly above plan despite a sharp reported revenue decline driven by planned channel and timing decisions. The launch of a new lower‑priced product line, Project Gravity, is progressing on plan and reinforces the brand’s effort to broaden its addressable market. A one‑time tariff refund provided an earnings tailwind, but the core narrative centers on resilient end‑market pull and a healthier retail environment, even as headline figures masked that strength.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership struck a confident tone, reiterating full‑year revenue guidance while raising the margin and adjusted EBITDA outlook, signaling conviction in improving operational leverage. The team continued to execute on a multi‑year cost‑reduction program, and the tariff refund was framed as a discrete benefit without altering the underlying trajectory. Management emphasized that sell‑through data, not reported shipments, offers the clearest gauge of business health, positioning the company as prudently navigating channel dynamics while delivering on new product milestones and maintaining credibility through a significant earnings beat.",
